# The step of the map scale_2, an array of two limbs times a scalar of T: mul_2_1 (milestone2.md:
# mul_2_1 when the scalar of scale is a T). Both come from the program; mul_2_1 only multiplies
# them, so rule R3 asks no guard. Its claims are those of mul_2_1.
kernel:        scale_step_2
input:         supplied x = x0 x1
input:         a
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         x*a
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=2 k=2 t=1
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v scale_step_2_correct
source:        mul_2_1 (JMP17 Alg. 9, DWTimesFP3); bound from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge spec

(z0, z1) = mul_2_1(x0, x1, a)
